{
  "caveats": [
    "Legit labels are not hand-audited: a Tranco site is labelled legit when it served a page and was on no keyless public blocklist (Phishing.Database ACTIVE list, OpenPhish feed); Google Safe Browsing was not used (no key configured).",
    "Phishing labels are the feed's own: a listed URL may already be dead or taken down; those are reported separately.",
    "Main-set phishing came from the OpenPhish feed that the live stack also ingests: a reputation lookup (T0) can catch these without any model. Read the main-set recall as feed-coverage plus pipeline, and use results_second_source (hosts from a feed the stack does not query) and the no_reputation_hit groups for the model's own detection.",
    "The same feed supplied the earlier training data, so the main phishing sample is not independent of it.",
    "23 URLs of the main set were submitted once in a discarded pilot of this same run before two extra fields were recorded; the raw rows were thrown away and all 200 were resubmitted, so those 23 may have been served from the verdict cache (latency).",
    "A request that hits the per-key rate limit waits for Retry-After and retries; latency_s includes that wait, http_429 counts the retries.",
    "Single run on one day, n=200; intervals are wide for subsets. Not a test-split result and not tuned on."
  ],
